1
00:00:00,007 --> 00:00:00,007
Gag (I’m not sure what Gya Gya Gya~~~ su means literally.)

2
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:08,367
Just a little more, Esra!

3
00:00:26,927 --> 00:00:28,567
How interesting…

4
00:00:28,567 --> 00:00:34,347
Never in a thousand years did I imagine a human being born with this kind of power was possible.

5
00:00:34,797 --> 00:00:36,847
It's truly... a miracle.

6
00:00:42,037 --> 00:00:44,857
A child wielding miraculous power.

7
00:00:46,787 --> 00:00:49,727
Esra… you did well hanging in there.

8
00:00:52,777 --> 00:00:54,657
It's a beautiful baby boy.

9
00:00:55,607 --> 00:00:58,787
His name… is Sinbad.

10
00:01:04,787 --> 00:01:07,177
A child who will become king of the seven seas.

11
00:01:17,007 --> 00:01:18,557
Scenery I've never seen before…

12
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:21,067
Strange beasts…

13
00:01:22,117 --> 00:01:24,377
Humid and warm air...

14
00:01:25,067 --> 00:01:27,817
This is... a Dungeon!

15
00:01:31,827 --> 00:01:34,697
The Conquest of Dungeon Baal ・ Part 2

16
00:01:53,867 --> 00:01:55,137
Crap!

17
00:02:07,547 --> 00:02:09,157
Don't break formation!

18
00:02:10,007 --> 00:02:11,567
Move forward along the cliff!

19
00:02:19,857 --> 00:02:20,997
What the hell?

20
00:02:21,927 --> 00:02:24,837
A one-hundred-man unit… gone in a flash…

21
00:02:32,177 --> 00:02:35,007
In... In a place like this…

22
00:02:35,007 --> 00:02:36,557
Come at me, beast!

23
00:02:52,327 --> 00:02:53,527
Y-You!

24
00:02:56,117 --> 00:02:57,827
This way!

25
00:02:59,117 --> 00:03:00,117
Hurry up!

26
00:03:07,697 --> 00:03:11,427
But how did you get here before me?

27
00:03:12,257 --> 00:03:14,397
I was the first one to enter.

28
00:03:14,397 --> 00:03:16,637
You're the brat who refused to enlist.

29
00:03:16,637 --> 00:03:17,717
Don't do something you'll regret.

30
00:03:18,237 --> 00:03:19,347
Huh?

31
00:03:19,347 --> 00:03:20,917
I'm a soldier.

32
00:03:20,917 --> 00:03:25,437
There's no reason I should have been saved by an unpatriotic person who defies his own country.

33
00:03:25,437 --> 00:03:28,127
I don't care about your reasons.

34
00:03:28,127 --> 00:03:30,487
I saved your life, so deal with it.

35
00:03:30,897 --> 00:03:35,957
You didn't even bother to thank me.

36
00:03:35,957 --> 00:03:37,157
Look who's childish now.

37
00:03:37,867 --> 00:03:39,577
I’m childish?!

38
00:03:40,177 --> 00:03:44,037
Fine. I’ll explain things in terms that even commoners like you can understand.

39
00:03:44,467 --> 00:03:45,907
Burn it in your head.

40
00:03:45,907 --> 00:03:47,907
My beautiful name.

41
00:03:48,687 --> 00:03:51,267
I am the youngest of the Parthevia Empire's Dragul lineage,

42
00:03:51,267 --> 00:03:55,797
Son of General Draguliel Hendrius Nodomis Pertegomidus,

43
00:03:55,797 --> 00:03:57,977
Lieutenant of the Western Region Military Unit,

44
00:03:57,977 --> 00:04:03,847
Dragul Nol Henrius Govius Menudias Partenuvonomias Dumid Os Kartanon.

45
00:04:06,447 --> 00:04:07,787
Too long.

46
00:04:07,787 --> 00:04:09,067
I’ll shorten it to Drakon.

47
00:04:09,557 --> 00:04:10,687
Huh? What?

48
00:04:10,687 --> 00:04:12,437
I said I’ll just call you Drakon.

49
00:04:13,567 --> 00:04:14,307
That's rude!

50
00:04:14,307 --> 00:04:16,027
There’s no way I’ll remember all that!

51
00:04:16,027 --> 00:04:19,197
I'm just Sinbad, and that's all there is to it!

52
00:04:19,197 --> 00:04:21,077
How dare you mock the Dragul family name!

53
00:04:21,787 --> 00:04:22,447
Die!

54
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:37,437
Apparently…

55
00:04:37,437 --> 00:04:39,967
It looks like we don't have time to be messing around.

56
00:04:46,367 --> 00:04:47,857
Just look at the size of it.

57
00:04:49,547 --> 00:04:52,527
Is he the Dragon King or something?

58
00:04:54,117 --> 00:04:58,507
He just ate those he didn't like.

59
00:04:58,507 --> 00:05:01,757
Though he's a Dragon King, he resmbles a human King perfectly.

60
00:05:01,757 --> 00:05:04,287
Shut your mouth, you commoner!

61
00:05:05,337 --> 00:05:09,287
To proceed any further, you need to do something about him, huh?

62
00:05:10,127 --> 00:05:13,207
This is where we put our lives on the line.

63
00:05:13,207 --> 00:05:15,797
We're being tested.

64
00:05:17,297 --> 00:05:19,297
<i>Tested, you say?</i>

65
00:05:21,777 --> 00:05:24,147
Sinbad, was it?

66
00:05:24,147 --> 00:05:26,487
I'll make you my subordinate for now.

67
00:05:26,487 --> 00:05:26,807
Huh?

68
00:05:27,247 --> 00:05:30,877
Be my decoy. Distract him.

69
00:05:30,877 --> 00:05:34,017
While you do, I'll head for the door.

70
00:05:34,017 --> 00:05:38,107
This is a test of whether we can achieve our goal despite making sacrifices.

71
00:05:38,107 --> 00:05:40,067
It's a test of determination.

72
00:05:40,067 --> 00:05:41,607
Now, go!

73
00:05:41,607 --> 00:05:43,447
Hey, don't make decisions on your own.

74
00:05:44,097 --> 00:05:47,167
A commoner like you will be helping our country.

75
00:05:47,167 --> 00:05:48,457
Be honored.

76
00:05:48,877 --> 00:05:51,207
If you're killed in action, I'll give you a reward.

77
00:05:51,807 --> 00:05:53,827
Just stop it.

78
00:05:53,827 --> 00:05:56,557
You're really a fool of the military.

79
00:05:56,557 --> 00:06:00,087
How many people have died with that mindset?!

80
00:06:06,807 --> 00:06:08,307
Be brave and stay.

81
00:06:08,907 --> 00:06:11,367
Lay down your life for your country.

82
00:06:11,367 --> 00:06:13,607
That is the pride of the Parthevian army.

83
00:06:15,527 --> 00:06:17,817
Dying for your country means satisfaction.

84
00:06:47,287 --> 00:06:48,887
What troublesome geysers.

85
00:06:49,597 --> 00:06:53,107
I have no idea where they'll erupt next.

86
00:06:53,607 --> 00:06:56,437
And these baby dragons…

87
00:07:02,607 --> 00:07:03,897
The gates…

88
00:07:03,897 --> 00:07:05,367
If I can just open the gates!

89
00:07:16,937 --> 00:07:17,957
I did it!

90
00:07:17,957 --> 00:07:18,957
I made it to the gate!

91
00:07:20,247 --> 00:07:21,627
Now, open!

92
00:07:21,627 --> 00:07:24,387
Oh Gate, open!

93
00:07:29,187 --> 00:07:29,887
Why?

94
00:07:30,747 --> 00:07:32,027
But why?!

95
00:07:36,267 --> 00:07:37,957
These are…

96
00:07:47,207 --> 00:07:50,577
Open. Open, open, open, open!

97
00:08:06,507 --> 00:08:09,007
No… no way, this isn't happening.

98
00:08:09,467 --> 00:08:13,097
I'm definitely going to die.

99
00:08:14,437 --> 00:08:15,657
No, not yet…

100
00:08:16,317 --> 00:08:20,147
I don't want to die yet!

101
00:08:28,347 --> 00:08:33,077
<i>Serendine-sama, First Princess of the Parthevian Empire.</i>

102
00:08:33,077 --> 00:08:37,327
<i>Lieutenant General Barbarossa-sama, eldest of the Dragul Family Line, </i><i></i>

103
00:08:37,997 --> 00:08:39,607
<i>Congratulations.</i>

104
00:08:39,607 --> 00:08:45,177
<i>This marriage is the first step towards glory for the Parthevian Empire.</i>

105
00:08:46,927 --> 00:08:50,217
<i>Well said, my brother.</i>

106
00:08:51,057 --> 00:08:52,387
You moron!

107
00:08:54,147 --> 00:08:55,767
Hey, get a hold of yourself.

108
00:08:56,377 --> 00:08:58,357
Get up, or you'll die!

109
00:09:07,007 --> 00:09:08,047
Kill…

110
00:09:10,017 --> 00:09:11,897
...Kill me!

111
00:09:12,467 --> 00:09:15,527
Fearing the enemy while clinging to my position…

112
00:09:15,527 --> 00:09:18,667
I’ve failed as a soldier.

113
00:09:18,667 --> 00:09:20,377
Bullshit.

114
00:09:20,867 --> 00:09:22,667
Be brave and stay.

115
00:09:22,667 --> 00:09:25,347
Give your life for your country?

116
00:09:25,347 --> 00:09:28,387
What's wrong with not wanting to die?

117
00:09:29,017 --> 00:09:30,467
It's so obvious!

118
00:09:30,467 --> 00:09:33,057
You're a human before you're a soldier!

119
00:09:34,497 --> 00:09:36,557
Dying for your country like that…

120
00:09:36,557 --> 00:09:41,207
Have the empire, the army, saved the people at least once?

121
00:09:42,767 --> 00:09:47,947
A country exists to protect the people living in it.

122
00:09:47,947 --> 00:09:51,247
It shouldn't encourage war and pushing them to their deaths.

123
00:09:52,147 --> 00:09:56,127
A country that discards its people… isn't needed!

124
00:10:06,137 --> 00:10:07,487
I’m borrowing this.

125
00:10:08,797 --> 00:10:09,887
Hey, you!

126
00:10:11,417 --> 00:10:14,057
You hear that, Drakon?!

127
00:10:16,837 --> 00:10:20,557
Those with power making sacrifices for their surroundings.

128
00:10:20,947 --> 00:10:22,977
It's the sound of accepting punishment.

129
00:12:00,077 --> 00:12:01,437
It opened.

130
00:12:01,437 --> 00:12:02,857
Let's go.

131
00:12:03,517 --> 00:12:06,607
Just what the hell are you?!

132
00:12:08,047 --> 00:12:12,497
It’s not what I am. It’s who I am.

133
00:12:13,187 --> 00:12:15,887
I'm Sinbad the sailor!

134
00:12:26,917 --> 00:12:28,317
Sinbad…

135
00:12:28,877 --> 00:12:30,907
What a strange man.

136
00:12:30,907 --> 00:12:33,817
When you think he's an idiot who casts away his life,

137
00:12:33,817 --> 00:12:38,067
he's actually calmly analyzing the situation.

138
00:12:38,477 --> 00:12:42,577
He makes the right choices at the right time and place.

139
00:12:45,237 --> 00:12:48,547
A man that rides on the wave of fate.

140
00:12:54,677 --> 00:12:56,117
We're here, huh?

141
00:12:56,117 --> 00:12:58,377
This is the deepest part of the Dungeon.

142
00:12:58,377 --> 00:13:01,157
Is your face turning blue yet?

143
00:13:01,157 --> 00:13:03,667
You're breathing pretty heavily yourself.

144
00:13:03,667 --> 00:13:06,317
Speak for yourself! Don't your feet hurt from running so much?

145
00:13:06,317 --> 00:13:08,647
That's because some idiot put me in a position where I had to!

146
00:13:11,307 --> 00:13:14,737
However, I praise you for doing well, for a commoner.

147
00:13:14,737 --> 00:13:18,947
And I thought you were some spoiled kid, but you've got some backbone.

148
00:13:18,947 --> 00:13:21,237
But not as much as I do, though.

149
00:13:21,237 --> 00:13:23,287
That's my line.

150
00:13:27,297 --> 00:13:29,287
Everything's made of stone.

151
00:13:30,067 --> 00:13:32,747
Nothing seems off, though.

152
00:13:32,747 --> 00:13:36,797
No, it doesn't feel that way to me.

153
00:13:52,707 --> 00:13:54,887
My name is Baal.

154
00:13:54,887 --> 00:13:57,357
I am the Djinn of Wrath and Heroes.

155
00:13:58,547 --> 00:14:01,577
Who is to become king?

156
00:14:02,497 --> 00:14:06,447
<i>Is this what Yunan was talking about? The power to become a king?</i>

157
00:14:07,547 --> 00:14:12,977
<i>The power that the wizards were talking about. If I can present this to his Majesty...</i>

158
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:13,707
In that case…

159
00:14:14,777 --> 00:14:16,607
The one who'll become king…

160
00:14:16,607 --> 00:14:18,337
Is me!

161
00:14:20,477 --> 00:14:22,557
Don't interfere, Drakon.

162
00:14:22,557 --> 00:14:26,817
I'm here with official orders from the Imperial Royalty.

163
00:14:26,817 --> 00:14:27,347
Stand down.

164
00:14:27,897 --> 00:14:29,597
To hell with your official order.

165
00:14:30,087 --> 00:14:34,727
I won't give any more power to those who step over the innocent.

166
00:14:35,417 --> 00:14:36,607
I've decided.

167
00:14:37,257 --> 00:14:42,117
I'll change this country – no, this world – with my own hands!

168
00:14:43,747 --> 00:14:47,157
So in the end, we have to settle the score.

169
00:14:47,607 --> 00:14:50,297
I owe you for saving my life.

170
00:14:50,297 --> 00:14:53,917
But I'm still a Parthevian soldier.

171
00:14:54,327 --> 00:14:57,417
And I won't waver either.

172
00:14:58,877 --> 00:15:04,177
Let us see who shall become my master.

173
00:15:08,607 --> 00:15:09,907
You're pretty good.

174
00:15:09,907 --> 00:15:10,477
But still…!

175
00:15:16,337 --> 00:15:19,397
Sinbad, you may be strong, but

176
00:15:22,057 --> 00:15:24,487
I'm not weak either!

177
00:15:29,847 --> 00:15:30,867
Goodbye.

178
00:15:38,677 --> 00:15:41,797
It's true you're a better swordsman.

179
00:15:42,097 --> 00:15:46,547
But this isn't a battle of who's better with a sword!

180
00:15:51,387 --> 00:15:54,437
<i>I'm losing consciousness…</i>

181
00:15:57,007 --> 00:16:00,397
<i>I promise that this conquest for the Dungeon will be a success.</i>

182
00:16:00,927 --> 00:16:04,747
<i>I absolutely will not hurt Serendine-sama's name.</i>

183
00:16:10,127 --> 00:16:11,617
<i>Don't be so serious.</i>

184
00:16:11,617 --> 00:16:13,037
<i>Your forehead will get wrinkles.</i>

185
00:16:13,647 --> 00:16:17,947
<i>Besides, I'm known as the Venomous Spider Princess.</i>

186
00:16:17,947 --> 00:16:20,047
<i>What's there to hurt?</i>

187
00:16:20,857 --> 00:16:23,777
<i>I've taken a liking to having two names.</i>

188
00:16:23,777 --> 00:16:24,797
<i>Shoot a web.</i>

189
00:16:24,797 --> 00:16:27,517
<i>Weaken the opponent, and kill them.</i>

190
00:16:27,517 --> 00:16:32,057
<i>I'm exactly like a spider that never lets her prey get away.</i>

191
00:16:33,567 --> 00:16:37,937
<i>So in your case, I'm more tenacious than you think.</i>

192
00:16:37,937 --> 00:16:39,567
<i>That's why, Dragul…</i>

193
00:16:40,837 --> 00:16:42,067
<i>Dying is unforgivable.</i>

194
00:16:47,277 --> 00:16:49,967
I can't lose yet…

195
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:52,407
I haven't lost yet!

196
00:16:56,297 --> 00:16:57,617
I can…

197
00:16:58,527 --> 00:17:00,127
I can still keep going!

198
00:17:06,107 --> 00:17:07,487
<i>Brother.</i>

199
00:17:07,487 --> 00:17:11,567
<i>Serendine-sama is a beautiful, smart, and strong princess.</i>

200
00:17:11,567 --> 00:17:15,977
<i>I'm sure you got to know her plenty yesterday.</i>

201
00:17:16,407 --> 00:17:18,277
<i>I support you both from the bottom of my hea---</i>

202
00:17:18,277 --> 00:17:22,977
<i>Junior. Aren't you misunderstanding something? </i><i></i>

203
00:17:23,487 --> 00:17:26,557
<i>This engagement is just like a foolish festival.</i>

204
00:17:26,557 --> 00:17:33,137
<i>It's just so the Dragul family can rebuild this weakening country.</i>

205
00:17:33,137 --> 00:17:34,997
<i>So about the princess…</i>

206
00:17:35,377 --> 00:17:36,997
<i>I don't love her.</i>

207
00:17:39,217 --> 00:17:40,937
<i>I couldn't say anything.</i>

208
00:17:40,937 --> 00:17:42,887
<i>I couldn't do anything.</i>

209
00:17:42,887 --> 00:17:45,447
<i>I couldn't protect the princess,</i>

210
00:17:45,447 --> 00:17:49,507
<i>nor could I tell her my feelings, either.</i>

211
00:17:50,627 --> 00:17:52,137
It's frustrating.

212
00:17:57,967 --> 00:18:01,897
My own… My own weakness is frustrating.

213
00:18:02,597 --> 00:18:07,397
But even so, I have things to protect.

214
00:18:08,747 --> 00:18:10,137
I know.

215
00:18:10,137 --> 00:18:14,407
I have my own reasons for not losing, either.

216
00:18:16,067 --> 00:18:16,907
That's why…

217
00:18:23,887 --> 00:18:24,587
I…

218
00:18:25,087 --> 00:18:25,667
I…

219
00:18:35,307 --> 00:18:37,097
...can't lose!

220
00:18:46,237 --> 00:18:48,857
I win.

221
00:18:52,547 --> 00:18:54,867
I've bared witness.

222
00:18:54,867 --> 00:18:57,327
I now acknowledge you as my master.

223
00:18:57,997 --> 00:18:59,157
Receive this!

224
00:19:00,997 --> 00:19:05,037
This is the power that many have desired.

225
00:19:08,877 --> 00:19:11,127
The First Dungeon Baal

226
00:19:08,877 --> 00:19:11,127
The First Dungeon Baal

227
00:19:08,877 --> 00:19:11,127
The First Dungeon Baal

228
00:19:08,877 --> 00:19:11,127
The First Dungeon Baal

229
00:19:11,217 --> 00:19:14,297
Conquest Completed

230
00:19:11,217 --> 00:19:14,297
Conquest Completed

231
00:19:11,217 --> 00:19:14,297
Conquest Completed

232
00:19:11,217 --> 00:19:14,297
Conquest Completed

233
00:19:18,977 --> 00:19:20,327
It's a soldier.

234
00:19:20,327 --> 00:19:22,327
An unconscious soldier!

235
00:19:33,857 --> 00:19:37,487
Great job, young conqueror.

236
00:19:37,797 --> 00:19:39,907
You're now honored as a young soldier.

237
00:19:39,907 --> 00:19:41,587
You've done well.

238
00:19:41,587 --> 00:19:45,767
Now, please hand over the loot and the Dungeon's power.

239
00:19:45,767 --> 00:19:47,997
Don't lump me in with you lot.

240
00:19:48,487 --> 00:19:51,317
This power and treasure is something that I worked for.

241
00:19:51,317 --> 00:19:53,297
I'll never hand them over to you.

242
00:19:53,577 --> 00:19:55,087
What did you say?!

243
00:19:55,087 --> 00:19:56,887
He's rebelling against the empire!

244
00:19:56,887 --> 00:19:57,557
Get him!

245
00:20:01,727 --> 00:20:05,017
Aren't you going to use the power you just earned?

246
00:20:05,017 --> 00:20:06,277
Yunan!

247
00:20:06,277 --> 00:20:07,977
Oh, that's right.

248
00:20:07,977 --> 00:20:11,737
You don't know how to use those powers yet.

249
00:20:13,817 --> 00:20:17,697
Do you need my assistance already, master?

250
00:20:18,167 --> 00:20:19,247
A blue giant!

251
00:20:19,247 --> 00:20:21,627
What is that? A monster?!

252
00:20:21,627 --> 00:20:24,897
Now, follow what your heart is telling you.

253
00:20:26,297 --> 00:20:28,697
O spirit of wrath and heroes.

254
00:20:28,697 --> 00:20:31,357
I command you to slay a thousand-fold.

255
00:20:31,357 --> 00:20:36,087
Use my magoi and will to enhance your power.

256
00:20:37,247 --> 00:20:39,597
Come forth, Baal!

257
00:20:46,167 --> 00:20:48,397
This is… my power?!

258
00:20:48,397 --> 00:20:49,987
Sinbad.

259
00:20:53,057 --> 00:20:54,147
Yunan? What's going on?!

260
00:20:54,527 --> 00:20:57,047
It'll take two days by boat, right?

261
00:20:57,047 --> 00:20:58,657
This a service of goodwill from me.

262
00:21:15,317 --> 00:21:17,707
That was the first time I've ever flown.

263
00:21:17,707 --> 00:21:19,507
Sin-nii-chan?

264
00:21:20,127 --> 00:21:21,887
It really is Sin-nii-chan!

265
00:21:21,887 --> 00:21:23,607
I'm back, everyone.

266
00:21:23,607 --> 00:21:25,017
Where have you been?!

267
00:21:25,397 --> 00:21:26,147
I conquered a Dun—

268
00:21:26,147 --> 00:21:29,227
Where were you for two months, leaving Esra-san alone?!

269
00:21:46,767 --> 00:21:50,877
Dear… is that you?

270
00:21:50,877 --> 00:21:52,067
You're back.

271
00:21:53,907 --> 00:21:56,247
If I can see you,

272
00:21:56,247 --> 00:21:58,747
It means I must be going soon.

273
00:21:59,447 --> 00:22:03,057
You know, in that brief moment,

274
00:22:03,057 --> 00:22:07,557
when he took your sword and went on his adventure...

275
00:22:08,867 --> 00:22:13,067
He was happy, confident, and overdoing it like a fool.

276
00:22:14,417 --> 00:22:18,277
But he treasures his family and friends.

277
00:22:18,277 --> 00:22:23,557
He really is a kind child, just like you.

278
00:22:23,557 --> 00:22:26,077
But he's grown up now.

279
00:22:27,317 --> 00:22:29,957
I'm sure he's okay.

280
00:22:31,697 --> 00:22:34,207
I love you… Sin…

281
00:22:35,567 --> 00:22:37,467
<i>You've found it, haven't you?</i>

282
00:22:37,917 --> 00:22:39,837
<i>Something that only you can do.</i>

283
00:22:40,777 --> 00:22:45,097
<i>Go and do what you have to do.</i>

284
00:22:45,397 --> 00:22:47,727
<i>I'll be fine.</i>

285
00:24:32,827 --> 00:24:38,957
Since then, Sinbad's name spread far and wide throughout Parthevia.

286
00:24:39,507 --> 00:24:43,047
And when news of how the Dungeon that was challenged by over 10,000 men

287
00:24:43,047 --> 00:24:46,947
was conquered by a 14-year-old boy,

288
00:24:46,947 --> 00:24:50,967
the war-torn started to feel encouragement.

289
00:24:51,907 --> 00:25:01,367
On the other hand, the little commoner hero was seen as an eyesore to royalty.

290
00:25:08,997 --> 00:25:13,997
They couldn't allow him to do as he pleased.

291
00:25:14,367 --> 00:25:16,997
A plan to capture him was set up.

292
00:25:17,267 --> 00:25:18,297
Listen.

293
00:25:18,297 --> 00:25:22,137
Sinbad will surely take his leave from this point.

294
00:25:22,137 --> 00:25:24,007
Be sure to arrest him and bring him here.

295
00:25:24,337 --> 00:25:25,087
Yes ma'am!

296
00:25:25,087 --> 00:25:27,537
For the princess to have to come here herself…

297
00:25:27,537 --> 00:25:28,967
How deplorable.

298
00:25:28,967 --> 00:25:30,377
Don't say that.

299
00:25:30,377 --> 00:25:32,607
We don't have enough troops to send out right now.

300
00:25:32,607 --> 00:25:35,247
It's just me and my guards.

301
00:25:35,247 --> 00:25:36,767
Besides…

302
00:25:36,777 --> 00:25:39,607
We won't do your bidding anymore!

303
00:25:39,607 --> 00:25:42,827
Sinbad sold his treasures and bought a boat!

304
00:25:42,827 --> 00:25:47,127
Who would ever follow an incompetent idiot who's interested in nothing but war?!

305
00:25:47,127 --> 00:25:48,707
Go home, you dogs!

306
00:25:48,707 --> 00:25:49,687
Move!

307
00:25:56,527 --> 00:25:59,157
I won't allow you to insult my father.

308
00:25:59,157 --> 00:26:02,497
I'll cut off your tongue and set you on fire!

309
00:26:03,787 --> 00:26:04,417
Stop.

310
00:26:05,347 --> 00:26:06,417
That young boy…

311
00:26:07,067 --> 00:26:09,427
You're Sinbad, aren't you?

312
00:26:10,017 --> 00:26:14,137
Oh? I'm glad a pretty lady like you knows my name.

313
00:26:14,137 --> 00:26:17,437
How dare you! Don't you know who she is?

314
00:26:17,437 --> 00:26:22,937
This is Serendine-sama, First Princess of the Parthevian Empire!

315
00:26:23,307 --> 00:26:26,187
Parthevia's Venomous Spider Princess?!

316
00:26:26,547 --> 00:26:31,697
Let me show you what happens to people that treat me like a pampered lady.

317
00:26:32,067 --> 00:26:35,287
Unfortunately, I don't like hurting girls—

318
00:26:35,287 --> 00:26:36,577
Stop spouting off!

319
00:26:37,537 --> 00:26:39,577
You fight well for someone with a pretty face.

320
00:26:40,077 --> 00:26:42,417
But you can't beat me.

321
00:26:47,097 --> 00:26:51,927
Do you know why people call me the Venomous Spider Princess?

322
00:26:51,927 --> 00:26:55,857
I'm aware that people from other lands call me that.

323
00:26:55,857 --> 00:26:57,477
That being said…

324
00:27:00,037 --> 00:27:03,477
That's poison from Desert king spiders.

325
00:27:04,607 --> 00:27:06,147
What's so funny?

326
00:27:06,147 --> 00:27:08,987
Good thing I took this on the fly.

327
00:27:08,987 --> 00:27:11,157
That's the antidote!

328
00:27:13,297 --> 00:27:17,697
Don't tell me… he took it from my pocket back then?

329
00:27:20,747 --> 00:27:22,957
And with that, I'm taking her hostage.

330
00:27:22,957 --> 00:27:23,537
Stop it!

331
00:27:23,537 --> 00:27:26,117
Don't interfere until I get on my boat.

332
00:27:26,117 --> 00:27:27,907
Princess!

333
00:27:29,707 --> 00:27:31,967
Damn you, put me down!

334
00:27:33,027 --> 00:27:33,967
What are you doing?!

335
00:27:34,387 --> 00:27:37,717
How dare you put me through this kind of embarrassment!

336
00:27:38,387 --> 00:27:42,937
S-Stay back. Don't touch me!

337
00:27:44,217 --> 00:27:45,357
Stop!

338
00:27:50,217 --> 00:27:53,267
Your soldiers can fetch you from this distance, right?

339
00:27:53,267 --> 00:27:57,327
Thanks for letting me take you hostage, pretty lady.

340
00:27:58,697 --> 00:28:03,867
Never... I'll never forgive you, Sinbad!

341
00:28:05,857 --> 00:28:07,997
Let's go.

342
00:28:09,017 --> 00:28:10,837
I'm going to change the world!

